Let me redo this. In K_{n,n} \ S, a right vertex v is a neighbor of left vertex u iff (u,v) ∉ S. The set of right neighbors of U in K_{n,n}\S is:
N(U) = {v ∈ V_right : ∃u ∈ U such that (u,v) ∉ S}
= V_right \ {v : for all u ∈ U, (u,v) ∈ S}
= V_right \ ⋂_{u∈U} S(u)

S₁ = {1, 2, 3}, allowed: {4}
S₂ = {2, 3, 4}, allowed: {1}
S₃ = {3, 4, 1}, allowed: {2}
S₄ = {4, 1, 2}, allowed: {3}
